course: dictionary
lesson: 7015
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word park can be a noun, a place, or a verb, an action. «At skate parks one rider goes in the bowl at a time» is about a place to skate, not about a garden.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A girl ran out between two parked vans» uses parked as a verb: the vans were stopped and left in one place. The clue is the vans. Cars and bikes can be parked, but a park cannot be parked.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think park means a green place with grass and trees, put that in: «A boy ate berries from a bush in the green place with grass and trees.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A noun names a thing or place. A verb is an action word.
fact: Park as a noun: a public green place with grass and trees where people play, walk and relax.
fact: Park as a verb: to stop a car or bike and leave it in a place.
fact: A national park is a large wild area kept safe for nature. A theme park or water park is a place with rides.
fact: Some phrases use park with a special meaning: «car park» (UK) and «parking lot» (USA) both mean a place to leave cars.
exercise: «At skate parks one rider goes in the bowl at a time.» What is a skate park? | *A place for skating, with ramps and bowls | A shop that sells skates | A car park for vans | A park with a big lake
exercise: «A girl ran out between two parked vans.» What does parked mean here? | Driving very fast | Painted in bright colours | Hidden under a tree | *Stopped and left in one place
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a green place with grass and trees: «Trees were planted in the park, and people sat on the grass.» | *park | planted | trees | people
test: Ella says park only means a green place. Is she right? | No, park is always a verb | Yes, park means a theme park only | *No, park can also be a verb: to park is to leave a car or bike somewhere | Yes, park only ever means a green place
test: «A national park is kept safe for nature.» What is a national park? | *A large wild area kept safe for nature | A small playground in a town | A car park by the shops | A water park with rides
exam: In «He parked his bike by the gate, then walked into the park.» which word is a verb? | *parked | the | gate | bike
